  parent: gru_v003
  status: finished
description: 'THIRD-PARTY RECIPE: soft mask on likely-scored rows + periodic state
  reset, on top of the best scoring base (v003).'
hypothesis: 'Scored rows are a distinct regime (0.58 WP on them vs 0.30 on all rows),
  so a loss weighted by P(is_scored) should help. Separately the recurrent state degrades
  over 20k rows (Q1 0.70 -> Q4 0.638) and a zero state beats the model''s own 10k-row
  state, so resetting every 4,000 rows during training AND inference should make the
  model emit a consistent level from a fresh state at any position. Together these
  are dozken/wunder''s best-scoring recipe. CONFOUNDED by design: if it wins we will
  not know which half did it, and a single-variable follow-up (v012) must attribute
  it.'
change_vs_parent: 'Two changes off gru_v003: (1) loss.mask_model=cache/train_scored.npy,
  a P(is_scored) predictor from tools/train_mask_model.py, weighting the loss toward
  rows likely to be scored - TRAINING-ONLY, no inference cost. (2) training.state_reset=4000
  and inference.state_reset=4000, the periodic recurrent-state reset, wired into the
  ONNX solution so it ships.'
